slacker-flatpak data
====================

Files installed with the binary:

  data/nl.slackware.forge.rizitis.SlackerFlatpak.desktop
                                      -> /usr/share/applications/
  data/icons/hicolor/                 -> /usr/share/icons/hicolor/

  e.g. in a SlackBuild:
    install -Dm755 target/release/slacker-flatpak $PKG/usr/bin/slacker-flatpak
    install -Dm644 data/nl.slackware.forge.rizitis.SlackerFlatpak.desktop \
      $PKG/usr/share/applications/nl.slackware.forge.rizitis.SlackerFlatpak.desktop
    mkdir -p $PKG/usr/share/icons
    cp -a data/icons/hicolor $PKG/usr/share/icons/

No polkit policy: slacker-flatpak never runs pkexec. Changes to the
system-wide Flatpak go through flatpak's own system helper and its polkit
rules.

Icons: 16, 22, 24, 32, 48, 64, 128, 256, 512 px PNG plus scalable SVG, all
named nl.slackware.forge.rizitis.SlackerFlatpak. 16-24 px come from a
simplified drawing (data/icons/source/slacker-flatpak-small.svg); the rest and
the scalable icon from data/icons/source/slacker-flatpak.svg. To regenerate:
    for s in 16 22 24; do rsvg-convert -w $s -h $s data/icons/source/slacker-flatpak-small.svg \
      -o data/icons/hicolor/${s}x${s}/apps/nl.slackware.forge.rizitis.SlackerFlatpak.png; done
    for s in 32 48 64 128 256 512; do rsvg-convert -w $s -h $s data/icons/source/slacker-flatpak.svg \
      -o data/icons/hicolor/${s}x${s}/apps/nl.slackware.forge.rizitis.SlackerFlatpak.png; done
    cp data/icons/source/slacker-flatpak.svg \
      data/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/nl.slackware.forge.rizitis.SlackerFlatpak.svg
Run uninstalled, the window finds no icon; that is expected.
